{=============================================================================
  Shell-and-tube mechanical sizing: tube counts, bundle diameters, TEMA rules
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0110 (function library, kind = function)
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Thirteen EES FUNCTIONs for the mechanical sizing of a shell-and-tube heat
  exchanger, transcribed from the Python library ht: TEMA tubing check,
  minimum bundle diameter, shell-bundle clearance, baffle and support-plate
  thickness, baffle hole diameter, maximum unsupported tube length, tube
  counts of Perry's Handbook, VDI Heat Atlas and HEDH with their bundle-
  diameter inverses, and the two method dispatchers Ntubes and
  size_bundle_from_tubecount.

  Lengths are in m; Ntp (tube passes), angle (layout, degrees) and the tube
  counts are dimensionless. The string options of ht (service, material,
  Method) became integer flags, documented at each function. Python int()
  truncation became FLOOR (the counts are positive). The methods needing
  data files are excluded: get_tube_TEMA (BWG table), Ntubes_Phadkeb and
  DBundle_for_Ntubes_Phadkeb (binary .npy coefficient tables).

  The demonstration program calls every function, once with the inputs of
  the ht doctest ("A" cases) and once with a second input set ("B"); the ht
  values of both sets are tabulated in the README (verification table).

  Inputs : Do, DBundle, DShell, pitch, L_unsupported [m], N, Ntp [-],
           angle [degrees], flags [-]
  Outputs: lengths/diameters [m], tube counts [-]
  Source : ht (Caleb Bell), ht/hx.py, version 1.2.0, commit 85e0ee6,
           MIT - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht ; original sources cited in
           each function block - see README.md
  Status : VERIFIED against the doctests and the values of ht 1.2.0
           (README.md, "Verification")
=============================================================================}

FUNCTION check_tubing_TEMA(NPS, BWG)
{CHECK_TUBING_TEMA - Is the (NPS, BWG) tubing combination listed by TEMA?
Returns 1 (listed) or 0 (not listed); ht returns a Boolean.

  NPS: nominal pipe size designation [inch, per the TEMA tables: 0.25, 0.375,
       0.5, 0.625, 0.75, 0.875, 1, 1.25, 2]
  BWG: Birmingham wire gauge of the wall [-] (10..24 as listed per NPS)
The listed combinations are the TEMA_tubing table of ht, one test per row.

Validity: as in the TEMA tables (no formula; pure table check).
Original: Standards of the Tubular Exchanger Manufacturers Association,
  Ninth edition, 2007, TEMA, New York.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/hx.py, check_tubing_TEMA,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  check_tubing_TEMA = 0
  IF (NPS = 0.25 AND BWG = 22) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.25 AND BWG = 24) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.375 AND BWG = 18) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.375 AND BWG = 20) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.375 AND BWG = 22) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.5 AND BWG = 18) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.5 AND BWG = 20) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.625 AND BWG = 16) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.625 AND BWG = 18) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.625 AND BWG = 20) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.75 AND BWG = 12) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.75 AND BWG = 14) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.75 AND BWG = 16) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.75 AND BWG = 18) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.75 AND BWG = 20) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.875 AND BWG = 14) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.875 AND BWG = 16) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.875 AND BWG = 18) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 0.875 AND BWG = 20) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 1 AND BWG = 12) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 1 AND BWG = 14) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 1 AND BWG = 16) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 1 AND BWG = 18) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 1.25 AND BWG = 10) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 1.25 AND BWG = 12) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 1.25 AND BWG = 14) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 1.25 AND BWG = 16) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 2 AND BWG = 12) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
  IF (NPS = 2 AND BWG = 14) THEN check_tubing_TEMA = 1
END

FUNCTION DBundle_min(Do)
{DBUNDLE_MIN - Roughly, a good initial choice of bundle diameter for a given
tube outer diameter, from figure 1, section 3.3.5 of the HEDH (a lookup, not a
correlation); the shell size is adjusted later once the area is known.

  Do <= 0.006 or <= 0.010 m -> DBundle_min = 0.1 m
  Do <= 0.014 m -> 0.3 m; Do <= 0.020 m -> 0.5 m; Do <= 0.030 m -> 1.0 m;
  Do > 0.030 m -> 1.5 m

Validity: rough guidance only, as in the original (essentially a lookup).
Original: Schlunder, E. U. and International Center for Heat and Mass
  Transfer, Heat Exchanger Design Handbook (HEDH), Hemisphere, Washington,
  1983, section 3.3.5, figure 1.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/hx.py, DBundle_min,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  DBundle_min = 0.1
  IF (Do > 0.010) THEN DBundle_min = 0.3
  IF (Do > 0.014) THEN DBundle_min = 0.5
  IF (Do > 0.020) THEN DBundle_min = 1.0
  IF (Do > 0.030) THEN DBundle_min = 1.5
END

FUNCTION shell_clearance(mode, D)
{SHELL_CLEARANCE - Recommended clearance between the shell and the tube
bundle of a TEMA exchanger (limits extended up to the next limit where
intermediate limits are not provided, as in ht).

  mode = 1: D is the shell inner diameter DShell [m]
  mode = 0: D is the outer bundle diameter DBundle [m]
  returns the clearance c [m]

DShell thresholds: < 0.457 -> 0.0032, < 1.016 -> 0.0048, < 1.397 -> 0.0064,
< 1.778 -> 0.0079, < 2.159 -> 0.0095, otherwise 0.011. The DBundle
thresholds are the DShell ones minus the clearance of the next limit:
0.4522, 1.0096, 1.3891, 1.7685, 2.148, otherwise 0.011.
Validity: TEMA shell sizes; pure table, no formula.
Original: Standards of the Tubular Exchanger Manufacturers Association,
  Ninth edition, 2007, TEMA, New York.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/hx.py, shell_clearance,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  c = 0.0095
  IF (D < 1.778) THEN c = 0.0079
  IF (D < 1.397) THEN c = 0.0064
  IF (D < 1.016) THEN c = 0.0048
  IF (D < 0.457) THEN c = 0.0032
  IF (D >= 2.159) THEN c = 0.011
  IF (mode = 0) THEN
    c = 0.0095
    IF (D < 1.7685) THEN c = 0.0079
    IF (D < 1.3891) THEN c = 0.0064
    IF (D < 1.0096) THEN c = 0.0048
    IF (D < 0.4522) THEN c = 0.0032
    IF (D >= 2.148) THEN c = 0.011
  ENDIF
  shell_clearance = c
END

FUNCTION baffle_thickness(Dshell, L_unsupported, service)
{BAFFLE_THICKNESS - Thickness of (latitudinal) baffles and support plates of
a TEMA exchanger; not for longitudinal baffles parallel to the tubes. The
pressure is almost the same on both sides of a baffle; L_unsupported is a
design choice (more baffles = higher pressure drop), as in the original.

  Dshell [m] shell inner diameter, L_unsupported [m] distance between tube
  supports, service = 1 for TEMA "R" (refinery), 0 for "C" and "B" (ht: any
  other string). Returns the baffle thickness [m].

Shell class j: Dshell < 0.381 -> 0, < 0.737 -> 1, < 0.991 -> 2,
< 1.524 -> 3, otherwise 4. Support class i (R): L <= 0.61 -> 0,
<= 0.914 -> 1, <= 1.219 -> 2, <= 1.524 -> 3, else 4. Support class i (C/B):
<= 0.305 -> 0, <= 0.610 -> 1, <= 0.914 -> 2, <= 1.219 -> 3, <= 1.524 -> 4,
else 5. Thickness tables (m), rows j, columns i:
  R: [0.0032 0.0048 0.0064 0.0095 0.0095; 0.0048 0.0064 0.0095 0.0095
      0.0127; 0.0064 0.0075 0.0095 0.0127 0.0159; 0.0064 0.0095 0.0127
      0.0159 0.0159; 0.0095 0.0127 0.0159 0.0191 0.0191]
  C/B: [0.0016 0.0032 0.0048 0.0064 0.0095 0.0095; 0.0032 0.0048 0.0064
        0.0095 0.0095 0.0127; 0.0048 0.0064 0.0075 0.0095 0.0127 0.0159;
        0.0064 0.0064 0.0095 0.0127 0.0159 0.0159; 0.0064 0.0095 0.0127
        0.0127 0.0191 0.0191]
Validity: TEMA shell sizes (no check implemented, as in ht).
Original: Standards of the Tubular Exchanger Manufacturers Association,
  Ninth edition, 2007, TEMA, New York.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/hx.py, baffle_thickness,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  j = 0
  IF (Dshell >= 0.381) THEN j = 1
  IF (Dshell >= 0.737) THEN j = 2
  IF (Dshell >= 0.991) THEN j = 3
  IF (Dshell >= 1.524) THEN j = 4
  IF (service = 1) THEN
    i = 0
    IF (L_unsupported > 0.61) THEN i = 1
    IF (L_unsupported > 0.914) THEN i = 2
    IF (L_unsupported > 1.219) THEN i = 3
    IF (L_unsupported > 1.524) THEN i = 4
  ELSE
    i = 0
    IF (L_unsupported > 0.305) THEN i = 1
    IF (L_unsupported > 0.610) THEN i = 2
    IF (L_unsupported > 0.914) THEN i = 3
    IF (L_unsupported > 1.219) THEN i = 4
    IF (L_unsupported > 1.524) THEN i = 5
  ENDIF
  k = 5*j + i
  IF (service = 0) THEN k = 6*j + i
  IF (service = 1) THEN
    baffle_thickness = 0.0032
    IF (k >= 1) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0048
    IF (k >= 2) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0064
    IF (k >= 3) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0095
    IF (k >= 4) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0095
    IF (k >= 5) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0048
    IF (k >= 6) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0064
    IF (k >= 7) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0095
    IF (k >= 8) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0095
    IF (k >= 9) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0127
    IF (k >= 10) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0064
    IF (k >= 11) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0075
    IF (k >= 12) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0095
    IF (k >= 13) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0127
    IF (k >= 14) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0159
    IF (k >= 15) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0064
    IF (k >= 16) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0095
    IF (k >= 17) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0127
    IF (k >= 18) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0159
    IF (k >= 19) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0159
    IF (k >= 20) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0095
    IF (k >= 21) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0127
    IF (k >= 22) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0159
    IF (k >= 23) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0191
    IF (k >= 24) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0191
  ELSE
    baffle_thickness = 0.0016
    IF (k >= 1) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0032
    IF (k >= 2) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0048
    IF (k >= 3) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0064
    IF (k >= 4) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0095
    IF (k >= 5) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0095
    IF (k >= 6) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0032
    IF (k >= 7) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0048
    IF (k >= 8) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0064
    IF (k >= 9) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0095
    IF (k >= 10) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0095
    IF (k >= 11) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0127
    IF (k >= 12) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0048
    IF (k >= 13) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0064
    IF (k >= 14) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0075
    IF (k >= 15) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0095
    IF (k >= 16) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0127
    IF (k >= 17) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0159
    IF (k >= 18) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0064
    IF (k >= 19) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0064
    IF (k >= 20) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0095
    IF (k >= 21) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0127
    IF (k >= 22) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0159
    IF (k >= 23) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0159
    IF (k >= 24) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0064
    IF (k >= 25) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0095
    IF (k >= 26) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0127
    IF (k >= 27) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0127
    IF (k >= 28) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0191
    IF (k >= 29) THEN baffle_thickness = 0.0191
  ENDIF
END

FUNCTION D_baffle_holes(Do, L_unsupported)
{D_BAFFLE_HOLES - Diameter of the tube holes in baffles, TEMA (applies for
all geometries): the clearance is 0.8 mm for tubes over 1-1/4 inch
(Do > 0.0318 m) or short unsupported spans (L_unsupported <= 0.914 m), and
0.4 mm otherwise, as in the original.

  Do [m] tube outer diameter, L_unsupported [m] distance between tube
  supports; returns the baffle hole diameter [m].

Validity: TEMA, all geometries (no range quoted).
Original: Standards of the Tubular Exchanger Manufacturers Association,
  Ninth edition, 2007, TEMA, New York.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/hx.py, D_baffle_holes,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  IF (Do > 0.0318 OR L_unsupported <= 0.914) THEN
    extra = 0.0008
  ELSE
    extra = 0.0004
  ENDIF
  D_baffle_holes = Do + extra
END

FUNCTION L_unsupported_max(Do, material)
{L_UNSUPPORTED_MAX - Maximum length a tube may span without a support, TEMA
limits for the worst-case temperature of the material.

  Do [m] tube outer diameter, material = 0 for "CS" (also high/low alloy
  steel, Ni-Cu, Ni, Ni-Cr-Fe alloys), 1 for "aluminium" (also Cu and Cu
  alloys, Ti alloys). Returns the maximum unsupported length [m].

The tabulated diameters [inch] are 0.25, 0.375, 0.5, 0.628, 0.75, 0.875, 1,
1.25, 1.5, 2, 2.5, 3; the result is that of the largest tabulated diameter
equal or smaller than Do (limits then not optimistic); below 1/4 inch the
result IS optimistic, above 3 inch the 3 inch limit applies (as in ht).
Tabulated lengths [m]: CS 0.66, 0.889, 1.118, 1.321, 1.524, 1.753, 1.88,
2.235, 2.54, 3.175, 3.175, 3.175; aluminium 0.559, 0.762, 0.965, 1.143,
1.321, 1.524, 1.626, 1.93, 2.21, 2.794, 2.794, 2.794.
Validity: 1/4 inch <= Do <= 3 inch (optimistic outside, as in ht).
Original: Standards of the Tubular Exchanger Manufacturers Association,
  Ninth edition, 2007, TEMA, New York, p 5.4-5.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/hx.py, L_unsupported_max,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  Do_inch = Do/0.0254
  Lcs = 0.66
  IF (Do_inch >= 0.375) THEN Lcs = 0.889
  IF (Do_inch >= 0.5) THEN Lcs = 1.118
  IF (Do_inch >= 0.628) THEN Lcs = 1.321
  IF (Do_inch >= 0.75) THEN Lcs = 1.524
  IF (Do_inch >= 0.875) THEN Lcs = 1.753
  IF (Do_inch >= 1.0) THEN Lcs = 1.88
  IF (Do_inch >= 1.25) THEN Lcs = 2.235
  IF (Do_inch >= 1.5) THEN Lcs = 2.54
  IF (Do_inch >= 2.0) THEN Lcs = 3.175
  Lalum = 0.559
  IF (Do_inch >= 0.375) THEN Lalum = 0.762
  IF (Do_inch >= 0.5) THEN Lalum = 0.965
  IF (Do_inch >= 0.628) THEN Lalum = 1.143
  IF (Do_inch >= 0.75) THEN Lalum = 1.321
  IF (Do_inch >= 0.875) THEN Lalum = 1.524
  IF (Do_inch >= 1.0) THEN Lalum = 1.626
  IF (Do_inch >= 1.25) THEN Lalum = 1.93
  IF (Do_inch >= 1.5) THEN Lalum = 2.21
  IF (Do_inch >= 2.0) THEN Lalum = 2.794
  IF (material = 0) THEN
    L_unsupported_max = Lcs
  ELSE
    L_unsupported_max = Lalum
  ENDIF
END

FUNCTION Ntubes_Perrys(DBundle, Do, Ntp, angle)
{NTUBES_PERRYS - Rough tube count of Perry's Chemical Engineers' Handbook
(equation 11-74), claimed accuracy 24 tubes (ht: experience suggests 40,
often ~20 off). Pitch = 1.25*Do. C is a dimensionless bundle-size measure:
C = 0.75*DBundle/Do - 36 for the 30 and 60 degree layouts, C = DBundle/Do-36
for 45 and 90 degrees; then a quartic in C per number of tube passes Ntp:
  30/60 deg: Ntp=1: ((((a1*C+a2)*C+a3)*C+a4)*C+a5) with (a1..a5) =
    (-0.0006, -0.0078, 1.283, 74.86, 1298); Ntp=2: (-0.0005, -0.0071,
    1.234, 73.58, 1266); Ntp=4: (-0.0004, -0.0059, 1.180, 70.79, 1196);
    Ntp=6: (-0.0006, -0.0074, 1.269, 70.72, 1166)
  45/90 deg: Ntp=1: (0.0001, -0.0012, 0.3782, 33.52, 593.6); Ntp=2:
    (0.0001, -0.0013, 0.3847, 33.36, 578.8); Ntp=4: (0.0002, -0.0016,
    0.3661, 33.04, 562.0); Ntp=6: (0.0001, -0.0013, 0.3873, 32.49, 550.4)
  returns FLOOR(Nt), the Python int() truncation of ht.
Validity: Ntp = 1, 2, 4 or 6; angle = 30, 45, 60 or 90 degrees.
Original: Green, D. W. and R. H. Perry, Perry's Chemical Engineers'
  Handbook, Eighth Edition, McGraw-Hill, New York, 2007, equation 11-74.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/hx.py, Ntubes_Perrys,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  tri = 0
  IF (angle = 30) THEN tri = 1
  IF (angle = 60) THEN tri = 1
  IF (tri = 1) THEN
    C = 0.75*DBundle/Do - 36
    IF (Ntp = 1) THEN Nt = ((((-0.0006)*C - 0.0078)*C + 1.283)*C + 74.86)*C + 1298
    IF (Ntp = 2) THEN Nt = ((((-0.0005)*C - 0.0071)*C + 1.234)*C + 73.58)*C + 1266
    IF (Ntp = 4) THEN Nt = ((((-0.0004)*C - 0.0059)*C + 1.180)*C + 70.79)*C + 1196
    IF (Ntp = 6) THEN Nt = ((((-0.0006)*C - 0.0074)*C + 1.269)*C + 70.72)*C + 1166
  ELSE
    C = DBundle/Do - 36
    IF (Ntp = 1) THEN Nt = ((((0.0001)*C - 0.0012)*C + 0.3782)*C + 33.52)*C + 593.6
    IF (Ntp = 2) THEN Nt = ((((0.0001)*C - 0.0013)*C + 0.3847)*C + 33.36)*C + 578.8
    IF (Ntp = 4) THEN Nt = ((((0.0002)*C - 0.0016)*C + 0.3661)*C + 33.04)*C + 562.0
    IF (Ntp = 6) THEN Nt = ((((0.0001)*C - 0.0013)*C + 0.3873)*C + 32.49)*C + 550.4
  ENDIF
  Ntubes_Perrys = FLOOR(Nt)
END

FUNCTION Ntubes_VDI(DBundle, Ntp, Do, pitch, angle)
{NTUBES_VDI - Rough tube count of the VDI Heat Atlas (rearranged form of the
original equation; the count is rounded down). Layout factor f1 = 1.1 for
the 30 and 60 degree layouts, 1.3 for 45 and 90; pass factor f2 = 0, 22, 70,
90, 105 for Ntp = 1, 2, 4, 6, 8 (the f2 = 90 of Ntp = 6 is an estimate added
by ht, the original has 1, 2, 4 and 8 only). With DBundle, Do, pitch in mm
(the equation is dimensional):
  S  = (-4*f1*t^4*f2^2*Do + 4*f1*t^4*f2^2*DBundle^2 + t^4*f2^4)^0.5
  N  = (-S - 2*f1*t^2*Do + 2*f1*t^2*DBundle^2 + t^2*f2^2)/(2*f1^2*t^4)
  returns FLOOR(N)
Validity: Ntp = 1, 2, 4, 6 (estimated) or 8; angle = 30, 45, 60, 90 degrees.
Original: Gesellschaft, V. D. I., ed., VDI Heat Atlas, 2nd edition,
  Springer, Berlin; New York, 2010.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/hx.py, Ntubes_VDI,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  f2 = 0
  IF (Ntp = 2) THEN f2 = 22
  IF (Ntp = 4) THEN f2 = 70
  IF (Ntp = 8) THEN f2 = 105
  IF (Ntp = 6) THEN f2 = 90
  f1 = 1.1
  IF (angle = 45 OR angle = 90) THEN f1 = 1.3
  DB_mm = DBundle*1000
  Do_mm = Do*1000
  t = pitch*1000
  S = (-4*f1*t^4*f2^2*Do_mm + 4*f1*t^4*f2^2*DB_mm^2 + t^4*f2^4)^0.5
  Nt = (-S - 2*f1*t^2*Do_mm + 2*f1*t^2*DB_mm^2 + t^2*f2^2)/(2*f1^2*t^4)
  Ntubes_VDI = FLOOR(Nt)
END

FUNCTION D_for_Ntubes_VDI(N, Ntp, Do, pitch, angle)
{D_FOR_NTUBES_VDI - Bundle diameter (outer tube limit) fitted to N tubes by
the VDI Heat Atlas equation, the inverse of Ntubes_VDI. Same factors f1
(layout) and f2 (passes) as Ntubes_VDI; with Do, pitch in mm:
  DBundle = (f1*N*t^2 + f2*N^0.5*t + Do)^0.5, in m after /1000
Note: the ht code adds Do inside the root; the equation printed in its
docstring shows a subtraction there - the code is what reproduces its
doctest (0.5003600119829544) and is followed here, as in the original code.
Validity: Ntp = 1, 2, 4, 6 (estimated) or 8; angle = 30, 45, 60, 90 degrees.
Original: Gesellschaft, V. D. I., ed., VDI Heat Atlas, 2nd edition,
  Springer, Berlin; New York, 2010.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/hx.py, D_for_Ntubes_VDI,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  f2 = 0
  IF (Ntp = 2) THEN f2 = 22
  IF (Ntp = 4) THEN f2 = 70
  IF (Ntp = 8) THEN f2 = 105
  IF (Ntp = 6) THEN f2 = 90
  f1 = 1.1
  IF (angle = 45 OR angle = 90) THEN f1 = 1.3
  Do_mm = Do*1000
  t = pitch*1000
  D_for_Ntubes_VDI = (f1*N*t^2 + f2*N^0.5*t + Do_mm)^0.5/1000
END

FUNCTION Ntubes_HEDH(DBundle, Do, pitch, angle)
{NTUBES_HEDH - Rough tube count of the HEDH, one pass (ht: seems reasonably
accurate):
  N = FLOOR(0.78*(DBundle - Do)^2/(C1*pitch^2))
C1 = 13/15 (0.866) for the 30 and 60 degree layouts, 1 for 45 and 90.
Validity: single-pass bundles; angle = 30, 45, 60 or 90 degrees.
Original: Schlunder, E. U. and International Center for Heat and Mass
  Transfer, Heat Exchanger Design Handbook (HEDH), Hemisphere, Washington,
  1983.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/hx.py, Ntubes_HEDH,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  C1 = 13/15
  IF (angle = 45 OR angle = 90) THEN C1 = 1
  Dctl = DBundle - Do
  Ntubes_HEDH = FLOOR(0.78*Dctl*Dctl/(C1*pitch*pitch))
END

FUNCTION DBundle_for_Ntubes_HEDH(N, Do, pitch, angle)
{DBUNDLE_FOR_NTUBES_HEDH - Bundle diameter fitted to N tubes by the HEDH
relation, the inverse of Ntubes_HEDH (one pass), easily reversed from the
main formulation as in ht:
  DBundle = Do + (1/0.78)^0.5*pitch*(C1*N)^0.5
C1 = 13/15 (0.866) for the 30 and 60 degree layouts, 1 for 45 and 90.
Validity: single-pass bundles; angle = 30, 45, 60 or 90 degrees.
Original: Schlunder, E. U. and International Center for Heat and Mass
  Transfer, Heat Exchanger Design Handbook (HEDH), Hemisphere, Washington,
  1983.
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/hx.py, DBundle_for_Ntubes_HEDH,
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  C1 = 13/15
  IF (angle = 45 OR angle = 90) THEN C1 = 1
  DBundle_for_Ntubes_HEDH = Do + (1/0.78)^0.5*pitch*(C1*N)^0.5
END

FUNCTION Ntubes(DBundle, Do, pitch, Ntp, angle, Method)
{NTUBES - Tube count of a bundle by the method chosen with the Method flag
(the string dispatcher of ht; its default "Phadkeb" method needs binary
coefficient tables and is not translated):
  Method = 1: HEDH  (Ntubes_HEDH, one pass)
  Method = 2: VDI   (Ntubes_VDI, f2 = 90 for 6 passes is an estimate)
  Method = 3: Perry (Ntubes_Perrys, claimed accuracy 24 tubes)
  returns the tube count [-] of the chosen method.
Validity: those of the chosen method.
Original: see the three functions above (Perry 2007, VDI Heat Atlas 2010,
  HEDH 1983).
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/hx.py, Ntubes (dispatcher),
  MIT License, C. Bell - https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  IF (Method = 1) THEN
    Ntubes = Ntubes_HEDH(DBundle, Do, pitch, angle)
  ELSE
    IF (Method = 2) THEN
      Ntubes = Ntubes_VDI(DBundle, Ntp, Do, pitch, angle)
    ELSE
      Ntubes = Ntubes_Perrys(DBundle, Do, Ntp, angle)
    ENDIF
  ENDIF
END

FUNCTION size_bundle_from_tubecount(N, Do, pitch, Ntp, angle, Method)
{SIZE_BUNDLE_FROM_TUBECOUNT - Bundle diameter fitted to N tubes by the
method chosen with the Method flag (the string dispatcher of ht):
  Method = 1: HEDH  (DBundle_for_Ntubes_HEDH, one pass)
  Method = 2: VDI   (D_for_Ntubes_VDI)
The "Phadkeb" method of ht needs binary coefficient tables (not translated)
and its "Perry" method solves Ntubes_Perrys by iteration, which an EES
FUNCTION cannot do: in EES, make DBundle an unknown of the main program and
write Ntubes_Perrys(DBundle, Do, Ntp, angle) = N (implicit solve).
  returns the bundle diameter DBundle [m].
Validity: those of the chosen method.
Original: see the two functions above (VDI Heat Atlas 2010, HEDH 1983).
Taken from: ht 1.2.0 (commit 85e0ee6), ht/hx.py,
  size_bundle_from_tubecount (dispatcher), MIT License, C. Bell -
  https://github.com/CalebBell/ht}
  IF (Method = 1) THEN
    size_bundle_from_tubecount = DBundle_for_Ntubes_HEDH(N, Do, pitch, angle)
  ELSE
    size_bundle_from_tubecount = D_for_Ntubes_VDI(N, Ntp, Do, pitch, angle)
  ENDIF
END

"!Demonstration program: every function is called twice"
"It is ignored by the future $INCLUDE library:shell_and_tube_sizing (CS-FEAT-IMPORT)."
"Case A: the input set of the ht doctest of each function (published values)."
"Case B: a second input set, computed with the same ht functions."
"Both cases are tabulated against ht in the README (verification table)."

"Case A - ht doctest inputs"
check_tubing_TEMA_A = check_tubing_TEMA(2, 22)
check_tubing_TEMA_ok_A = check_tubing_TEMA(0.375, 22)
DBundle_min_A = DBundle_min(0.0254)
shell_clearance_A = shell_clearance(0, 1.245)
shell_clearance_DShell_A = shell_clearance(1, 1.9)
baffle_thickness_R_A = baffle_thickness(0.3, 50, 1)
D_baffle_holes_A1 = D_baffle_holes(0.0508, 0.75)
D_baffle_holes_A2 = D_baffle_holes(0.01905, 0.3)
D_baffle_holes_A3 = D_baffle_holes(0.01905, 1.5)
L_unsupported_max_A = L_unsupported_max(0.0254, 0)
Ntubes_Perrys_A = Ntubes_Perrys(1.184, 0.028, 2, 45)
Ntubes_VDI_A = Ntubes_VDI(1.184, 2, 0.028, 0.036, 30)
D_for_Ntubes_VDI_A = D_for_Ntubes_VDI(970, 2, 0.00735, 0.015, 30)
Ntubes_HEDH_A = Ntubes_HEDH(1.184, 0.028, 0.036, 30)
DBundle_for_Ntubes_HEDH_A = DBundle_for_Ntubes_HEDH(928, 0.028, 0.036, 30)
Ntubes_Perry_A = Ntubes(1.2, 0.025, 0.03125, 1, 30, 3)
Ntubes_VDIm_A = Ntubes(1.2, 0.025, 0.03125, 1, 30, 2)
Ntubes_HEDHm_A = Ntubes(1.2, 0.025, 0.03125, 1, 30, 1)
size_bundle_VDI_A = size_bundle_from_tubecount(1285, 0.025, 0.03125, 1, 30, 2)
size_bundle_HEDH_A = size_bundle_from_tubecount(1285, 0.025, 0.03125, 1, 30, 1)

"Case B - second input set"
check_tubing_TEMA_B = check_tubing_TEMA(1.25, 18)
check_tubing_TEMA_ok_B = check_tubing_TEMA(0.75, 16)
DBundle_min_B = DBundle_min(0.015)
shell_clearance_B = shell_clearance(0, 0.5)
shell_clearance_DShell_B = shell_clearance(1, 0.61)
baffle_thickness_C_B = baffle_thickness(1.2, 0.7, 0)
baffle_thickness_R_B = baffle_thickness(1.2, 0.7, 1)
D_baffle_holes_B = D_baffle_holes(0.0254, 1.2)
L_unsupported_max_alum_B = L_unsupported_max(0.01905, 1)
L_unsupported_max_cs_B = L_unsupported_max(0.03, 0)
Ntubes_Perrys_B = Ntubes_Perrys(0.8, 0.01905, 4, 30)
Ntubes_Perrys_90_B = Ntubes_Perrys(0.8, 0.01905, 2, 90)
Ntubes_VDI_B = Ntubes_VDI(0.8, 4, 0.01905, 0.025, 45)
Ntubes_VDI_1p_B = Ntubes_VDI(0.5, 1, 0.01905, 0.0238, 60)
D_for_Ntubes_VDI_B = D_for_Ntubes_VDI(500, 4, 0.01905, 0.0238, 60)
Ntubes_HEDH_B = Ntubes_HEDH(0.8, 0.01905, 0.0238, 90)
Ntubes_HEDH_tri_B = Ntubes_HEDH(0.5, 0.01905, 0.0238, 30)
DBundle_for_Ntubes_HEDH_B = DBundle_for_Ntubes_HEDH(600, 0.01905, 0.0238, 60)
Ntubes_Perry_B = Ntubes(0.8, 0.01905, 0.0238, 2, 30, 3)
Ntubes_VDIm_B = Ntubes(0.8, 0.01905, 0.0238, 2, 30, 2)
Ntubes_HEDHm_B = Ntubes(0.8, 0.01905, 0.0238, 2, 30, 1)
size_bundle_VDI_B = size_bundle_from_tubecount(800, 0.01905, 0.0238, 1, 30, 2)
size_bundle_HEDH_B = size_bundle_from_tubecount(800, 0.01905, 0.0238, 1, 30, 1)
